## Obiettivo

Uniformare la card del percorso guidato alla superficie neutra della Home React, mantenendo il verde come solo accento semantico.

## Modifiche

- superficie esterna da verde tenue a bianca;
- bordo esterno da verde a neutro;
- icona inserita nello stesso box ottico usato dalle altre card;
- verde mantenuto per icona, stato di avanzamento e CTA;
- nessuna modifica al dialogo, ai dati, alla persistenza, all’esportazione o alla logica del percorso.

## Nota di governance

La documentazione `docs/03_execution/CML-490.md` è già presente su `main`; questa PR contiene il solo delta runtime.

`CML_490_GUIDED_EVALUATION_NEUTRAL_SURFACE_MICROFIX_READY_FOR_REVIEW`

Removes the custom React lead form from `ResultView` (which posted to a Netlify function → GoHighLevel) and replaces it with an embedded LeadConnector iframe + a one-time external script loader.

### Changes

- **Imports:** Removed `AlertCircle` (lucide-react) and `callNetlifyFunction` (@/lib/api) — both now unused
- **ResultView state/logic deleted:** `leadForm`, `leadSubmitting`, `leadError`, `leadSuccess`, `updateLeadForm`, `submitLead`, `canSubmit`
- **Added** `useEffect` script loader (runs once, idempotent via `scriptId` guard):
  ```jsx
  useEffect(() => {
    const scriptId = "msgsndr-form-embed";
    if (document.getElementById(scriptId)) return;
    const script = document.createElement("script");
    script.id = scriptId;
    script.src = "https://link.msgsndr.com/js/form_embed.js";
    script.async = true;
    document.body.appendChild(script);
  }, []);
  ```
- **"Final Step" section** replaced with a static `<iframe>` pointing to `https://api.leadconnectorhq.com/widget/form/0vodT8LE8uNLmKeFbnvx`

## Summary

Polishes archive date entry across desktop and mobile while preserving the existing backend date model and all supported precision values.

Desktop now uses:

* native date inputs for exact dates and exact-date ranges;
* compact segmented inputs for year and month precision;
* side-by-side range controls where space allows.

Mobile uses compact numeric date rows for all precision types, avoiding native historical date pickers.

## Changes

* Added separate desktop and mobile date-entry representations.
* Added explicit precision groups for:

  * year;
  * month;
  * exact day;
  * year range;
  * month range;
  * exact-day range.
* Ensured only the active responsive representation and precision group are visible and enabled.
* Added responsive synchronization when crossing the mobile breakpoint.
* Added digit-only sanitization for segmented day, month, and year inputs.
* Preserved native desktop date inputs for exact-day entry.
* Replaced native desktop month controls with compact `MM / YYYY` inputs.
* Added unique HTML ids across all hidden and active date controls.
* Updated accessibility labels and grouped-control semantics.
* Added regression coverage for duplicate ids, active-field state, responsive markup, segmented month controls, and digit sanitization.

## Backend impact

No changes to:

* models;
* migrations;
* date normalization;
* storage semantics;
* public date display;
* supported precision values.

## Validation

* 109 focused tests passed.
* Ruff format passed.
* Ruff check passed.
* Django system check passed.
* `makemigrations --check --dry-run` reported no changes.
* `git diff --check` passed.

## Objectif

Remplacer uniquement la mascotte du thème **Memphis Productivity** par un personnage premium inspiré du concept fourni, compatible avec la promenade globale et le glisser-déposer existants.

## Réalisation

- nouveau rig SVG React composé d’une tête circulaire, d’un torse géométrique, de bras tubulaires, d’un gant, de jambes, de chaussures et de motifs Memphis ;
- expressions dédiées pour `idle`, `happy`, `celebrate`, `worried` et `sleepy` ;
- animations CSS continues : respiration, hochement de tête, salut, balancement des bras, pas alternés et pulsation des motifs ;
- séquences GSAP propres à `habit-done`, `perfect-day` et `streak-record` ;
- nettoyage systématique des transformations après chaque réaction ;
- respect de `prefers-reduced-motion` ;
- aucun changement du contrat des mascottes, de la promenade globale ou de la logique métier.

## Validation attendue

- contrôle d’architecture ;
- ESLint ;
- tests Vitest ;
- compilation TypeScript et build Vite ;
- smoke test Chromium.

## Périmètre

Seul le thème `memphis-productivity` est modifié. Les onze autres mascottes restent inchangées.

## What

Adds a new `applyChanges` method (and an `ObservableClient.Changes` type) to `@osdk/client`'s `ObservableClient`. It pushes externally-sourced object upserts and deletes straight into the observable cache that the `@osdk/react` / `@osdk/react-components` hooks read.

```ts
export namespace ObservableClient {
  export interface Changes {
    upserts?: ReadonlyArray<Osdk.Instance<ObjectOrInterfaceDefinition, "$allBaseProperties">>;
    deletes?: ReadonlyArray<{ objectType: string; primaryKey: string | number }>;
  }
}

interface ObservableClient {
  applyChanges(changes: ObservableClient.Changes): Promise<void>;
}
```

## How

It reuses the existing ingest paths rather than inventing a new one, all inside a single `Store.batch`:

- **upserts** go through `objects.storeOsdkInstances` -> `writeToStore` -> `propagateWrite`, the same path server page fetches and websocket stream updates use.
- **deletes** tombstone every registered cache variant of the object via `deleteFromStore` -> `propagateWrite` (the same path action-result deletes use). Objects that were never loaded have no registered variants and are ignored.

Because it runs in one batch, all observing hooks (objects, lists, object sets, links, dependent functions) update reactively without a network round trip.

## Why

This is the seam an embedded or offline ontology engine uses to stream locally-synced deltas into the hooks. Combined with the already-public `createClientWithSubscriptionConnection` (subscription transport), the `fetchFn` override on `createClient` (reads/writes), and `objectFactory` (wire to instance conversion), it lets such an engine drive every hook online and offline with live updates.

## Compatibility

Additive and non-breaking. Callers that never invoke `applyChanges` are unaffected. The `ObservableClient` interface lives on the `@osdk/client/observable` subpath, which is not part of the api-extractor main-entry report, so no API report changes.

## Testing

- New `Store.applyChanges.test.ts` (5 tests, FauxFoundry harness, `mode: "offline"`): upsert updates an observed object, upsert inserts a matching object into an observed list, delete removes an object from list + cache, combined upsert/delete in one batch, and empty no-op. All exercise cache-only updates with no network fetch.
- `pnpm turbo typecheck --filter=@osdk/client --filter=@osdk/react-devtools` passes.
- `pnpm turbo check-api --filter=@osdk/client`: report up to date.
- Full `@osdk/client` observable suite passes (356 passed, 1 skipped).

A changeset (`@osdk/client: minor`) is included.

## Summary

Completes the remaining evidence-integration slice of #222 on top of the merged structural-clustering (#319), held-out transfer (#323), open-target lifecycle (#221) and interestingness contract (#324).

### Paired cross-family ablation

Adds `CrossFamilyBridgeAblationEvaluator` and the versioned contract `regelsuche.cross-family-bridge-ablation/v1`.

- compares the same family tasks with and without an already formed bridge;
- requires exact formation/held-out family provenance from the accepted transfer report;
- distinguishes material gain, unchanged behavior, regression, metric trade-off and incomplete evidence per family;
- requires a material gain in at least one held-out family and forbids regressions before reporting `BENEFICIAL_HELD_OUT`;
- treats missing success or comparable path/state metrics as incomplete rather than beneficial;
- emits deterministic paired run evidence and a content hash.

### Independent bridge qualification

Adds `CrossFamilyBridgeQualificationGate` and `regelsuche.cross-family-bridge-qualification/v1`.

The gate binds one stable bridge identity across:

- target-free formation and accepted per-family transfer;
- lifecycle evidence at least `VALIDATED_BY_EXAMPLES` with unchanged patterns, assumptions, parameter relations and expression placeholders;
- project novelty from the existing exact/alpha checker;
- an eligible target-free symbolic proof obligation;
- beneficial held-out paired ablation;
- a complete, non-blocked interestingness assessment bound to the transfer report.

Truth, project novelty, external novelty, assumptions, proof, ablation and interestingness remain separate fields. The result is only `QUALIFIED_FOR_PROMOTION_REVIEW`; promotion and public evidence remain `NOT_EVALUATED` and continue to use their established gates.

### Characterization and retained evidence

Tests cover:

- a fully qualified bridge with complete family transfer, symbolic proof, project novelty and held-out utility;
- a held-out family with no material gain blocking qualification even when formation families improve;
- an active-inventory duplicate preserving proof evidence while blocking qualification;
- assumption drift across formation, lifecycle and proof evidence;
- deterministic reports under reversed family-ablation order.

Java CI now requires and uploads:

- `regelsuche-learning/build/reports/cross-family-bridge-qualification/ablation.json`
- `regelsuche-learning/build/reports/cross-family-bridge-qualification/report.json`

### Scientific boundary

This PR qualifies a bridge for the ordinary promotion-review stage. It does not itself insert a rule, publish public evidence, claim external mathematical novelty or replace a configured formal-proof policy.

Relates #222, #223, #226 and #235.

## Summary

Implements stage 1 of the native OLX PL integration:

- replaces the local `connected=true` toggle with a real authorization-code OAuth flow;
- stores workspace marketplace credentials encrypted with AES-256-GCM;
- uses short-lived, single-use Redis OAuth state keyed by a SHA-256 digest;
- refreshes expired OLX access tokens inside the publish worker;
- publishes adverts through the OLX Partner API (`POST /adverts`);
- resolves tokens by `marketplaceId` inside the worker, never in queue payloads;
- adds connect/check/callback UI and API contracts;
- adds persistence migrations and reconciles legacy false-connected OLX rows;
- documents the guarded live-publish runbook and stage boundary.

## Safety guarantees

- `OLX_ADAPTER_MODE=real` remains opt-in.
- `OLX_LIVE_PUBLISH_ENABLED=false` remains the default and fail-closes Partner create-advert requests.
- Non-idempotent publish jobs are configured for exactly one Bull attempt.
- Provider validation details are sanitized before persistence/logging.
- OAuth callback state is TTL-bound, one-time, provider/workspace-bound, and replay-resistant.
- Access/refresh tokens and client secrets are not exposed through browser DTOs, logs, or Redis job payloads.

## Verification

Local CI-equivalent verification on the final branch:

- backend typecheck: passed;
- frontend/full typecheck: passed;
- Jest: **229 passed**, 4 skipped, 32 suites passed (1 skipped);
- frontend production build: passed;
- backend production build: passed;
- `git diff --check`: passed;
- changed-source secret scan: no credentials or private keys found.

ESLint remains non-blocking exactly as configured in CI; the repository currently uses ESLint 10 without an `eslint.config.*` file, so the lint command exits before evaluating source files.

## Real provider validation

The guarded runtime path was exercised end-to-end against OLX PL:

1. browser authorization and callback completed;
2. encrypted `marketplace_accounts` credentials persisted;
3. publish preview returned no warnings;
4. one queue attempt created the advert;
5. local listing finalization persisted the provider ID and published timestamp;
6. authenticated Partner API readback succeeded;
7. provider status transitioned to `active`;
8. anonymous public readback returned HTTP 200.

Concrete seller/account/advert identifiers and contact details are intentionally omitted.

## Not included in stage 1

- scheduled polling or provider webhooks;
- account-scoped credential resolution in the existing manual sync worker;
- remote advert status reconciliation into local listing state;
- complete OLX taxonomy/attribute mapping for every category and location;
- long-lived production media hosting.


