## Summary

Fixes the TypeScript error where `ProductCard` expected `image` and `title` props but `ShoppingPage` was passing a `product` object.

- `ProductCard` now receives a single `product: ProductCardProps` prop and reads `product.image` / `product.title`.
- `ShoppingPage` builds two typed `ProductCardProps` objects and passes them as `product={...}`.

```tsx
interface ProductCardProps {
  id: string;
  image: string;
  title: string;
}

interface Props {
  product: ProductCardProps;
}

const ProductCard = ({ product }: Props) => { ... };
```

The production build (`npm run build`) now compiles successfully.

